INT. MUNICIPAL LOST PROPERTY OFFICE - DAY

A long basement room under a bus depot. Steel shelves labelled by month. Hundreds of umbrellas hang from the pipes like sleeping bats. A single fluorescent tube flickers over the counter.

DOREEN PALMQUIST, 60s, cardigan buttoned to the neck, reading glasses on a chain, sorts a tray of single gloves. Everything on her desk is squared to the edge.

PAULO MENDES-RIBEIRO, 30s, damp raincoat, a worn leather folder under his arm, stands at the counter. He has been standing there for some time.

DOREEN
Form 12-B.

PAULO
I filled in a 12-B.

DOREEN
You filled in a 12-A.

PAULO
They look the same.

DOREEN
They are not the same.

She hands him a form. He takes it. Uses the pen on the chain, which is short, so he has to lean over the counter to write.

PAULO
Colour of umbrella?

DOREEN
You tell me.

PAULO
Black.

Doreen turns slowly toward the shelves. Hundreds of black umbrellas.

DOREEN
Describe it.

PAULO
It's an umbrella.

She sets down the glove. Aligns it with the others.

DOREEN
Handle?

PAULO
Wooden. Duck head.

DOREEN
A duck.

PAULO
It was my father's.

Doreen's pen stops. Starts again.

DOREEN
Duck-handled. Black. Bus route?

PAULO
Forty-one.

DOREEN
Day?

PAULO
Tuesday. Or Wednesday.

Doreen removes her glasses. Lets them hang. Breathes through her nose.

GRANT HOLLIS, 20s, a high-vis vest over a suit, wheels in a cart of fresh umbrellas, humming. He drops the cart handle. It clangs.

GRANT
Got a batch off the forty-one.

Paulo and Doreen both look at the cart. A black umbrella, duck handle, on top.

PAULO
That's it.

DOREEN
That is a batch item. It is not yet logged.

PAULO
It's my father's.

DOREEN
It is not yet logged.

Paulo reaches. Doreen's hand lands flat on the umbrella first. Quick for sixty.

GRANT
(to the floor)
I could just log it?

DOREEN
You could not.

PAULO
Give me the umbrella.

DOREEN
Form 12-B.

Paulo tears the form in half. Then in half again. Lets the pieces fall onto the counter. Doreen watches them land.

She picks up a stamp. Brings it down on the first piece, hard. Then the second. Then the third. Thud. Thud. Thud.

GRANT
(backing the cart toward the door)
I'll come back.

DOREEN
Stay where you are, Mr. Hollis.

She lifts the umbrella by the duck's neck and holds it out across the counter, level, like a sword being surrendered.

DOREEN (CONT'D)
Sign for it.

Paulo takes it. His hand shakes. He signs the stamped paper with the chain pen, bent double over the counter, and the pen's bead chain snaps.

Everyone looks at the pen.
